  "spec_section": "protocol.md §9.8 + §3.4 + §5.2 + §6.4",
  "description": "Pins protocol::encode_vault_indices_blob_raw + protocol::decode_vault_indices_blob byte mapping for the MYI1 vault.indices encrypted structured-metadata codec (MYND-271; design MYND-31). The header's index_format_version is 0x02 as of MYND-612, which added per-note line-task records to the inner plaintext; 0x01 blobs are rejected rather than migrated, since the index is a rebuildable cache. The inner plaintext is OPAQUE (client-serialized structured index: wikilink graph + tag index + title map + typed property records + per-note line-task records) — no canonical-JSON discipline, unlike vault-prefs; the structural twin of vault.search/vault.workspace. vault_indices_key = derive_subkey(root_key, SubkeyRole::VaultIndicesKey) (role 'vault-indices-key'); account_number_hash binds via aad_vault_indices_blob (role 'vault-indices-blob' — a DISTINCT load-bearing string, and DISTINCT from search-index-key/-blob: one magic + one KEK per blob family, MYI1 != MYS1). 12 cases: 3 encrypt (empty / small descriptor / 1-KB) + 1 decrypt_ok + 2 decrypt_aead_fail (tag-tamper + cross-vault, both non-distinguishing per §6.4, real-key fixtures) + 6 parse_fail (one per distinguishable pre-decryption structural reject incl. the load-bearing format_unsupported forward hook). Cases generated by `cargo test -p protocol --lib emit_vault_indices_vectors_for_paste -- --ignored` (in protocol/src/vault_indices_blob.rs).",
